papers/29-functorial-chiral-counterterm-no-go/LITERATURE_AUDIT.md:64:The closest structural precedent is the non-backtracking graph determinant.  It removes immediate inverse-edge reversals by a graph-isomorphism-natural local rule and admits Bass's degree correction.  It does so by changing the admissible word system and transfer operator.  It is an ordinary finite determinant, the divisibility DAG has no native edge reversal, and it does not preserve the weighted mixed Gram phase.  This is a Round-2 clue, not an identity with the present counterterm.
